g (a)(b) = a(b - c + c) but not sure. Alternatively, use (700 + 60)(1000 - 2). Wait, maybe expanding that:\n\n(700 + 60)(1000 - 2) = 700*1000 + 700*(-2) + 60*1000 + 60*(-2)\n\nWhich is 700,000 - 1,400 + 60,000 - 120.\n\nAdding those: 700,000 + 60,000 = 760,000. Then -1,400 -120 = -1,520. So again, 760,000 -1,520 = 758,480. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so I think the correct answer is 758,480. The initial method the user mentioned had some numbers that didn't align with the problem, but my calculations here all confirm the same result. I'll go with that.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 760 and 998 is \\boxed{758480}.\n｜\n\nTo find the product of 760 and 998, we can use the distributive property by recognizing that 998 is close to 1000. \n\nFirst, rewrite 998 as \\(1000 - 2\\):\n\\[\n760 \\times 998 = 760 \\times (1000 - 2)\n\\]\n\nApply the distributive property:\n\\[\n760 \\times 1000 - 760 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part separately:\n\\[\n760 \\times 1000 = 760000\n\\]\n\\[\n760 \\times 2 = 1520\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\\[\n760000 - 1520 = 758480\n\\]\n\nVerification using standard multiplication:\n- Multiply 760 by 8: \\(760 \\times 8 = 6080\\)\n- Multiply 760 by 90: \\(760 \\times 90 = 68400\\)\n- Multiply 760 by 900: \\(760 \\times 900 = 684000\\)\n\nAdd the results:\n\\[\n6080 + 68400 + 684000 = 758480\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, the product of 760 and 998 is \\boxed{758480}.｜\nAssistant｜>｜\n\nTo find the product of 760 and 998, we can use the distributive property by recognizing that 998 is close to 1000. \n\nFirst, rewrite 998 as \\(1000 - 2\\):\n\\[\n760 \\times 998 = 760 \\times (1000 - 2)\n\\]\n\nApply the distributive property:\n\\[\n760 \\times 1000 - 760 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part separately:\n\\[\n760 \\times 1000 = 760000\n\\]\n\\[\n760 \\times 2 = 1520\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\\[\n760000 - 1520 = 758480\n\\]\n\nVerification using standard multiplication:\n- Multiply 760 by 8: \\(760 \\times 8 = 6080\\)\n- Multiply 760 by 90: \\(760 \\times 90 = 68400\\)\n- Multiply 760 by 900: \\(760 \\times 900 = 684000\\)\n\nAdd the results:\n\\[\n6080 + 68400 + 684000 = 758480\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, the product of 760 and 998 is \\boxed{758480}.｜", '']  1%|          | 3/500 [22:06<51:18:41, 371.67s/it]
